# Build context exclusions. Anything listed here is invisible to `docker build`, so it
# neither bloats the context nor busts the layer cache when it changes.

# Reinstalled inside the image from package-lock.json; a host copy would also carry
# linux-x64 vs. host-arch native binaries.
node_modules
.next
out
dist

# Local environment and credentials — must never reach an image layer.
# This is load-bearing, not hygiene: `next build` COPIES any .env it loads into
# .next/standalone/, which the runtime stage then ships. A developer's .env reaching
# the build context therefore ends up verbatim inside the published image.
# Nothing in the build needs .env.example either, so there is no negation here.
.env
.env.*
*.local.md

# VCS and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Tooling and tests — not needed to build or run the server.
# eslint.config.mjs is deliberately NOT excluded: `next build` resolves it if linting is
# enabled, and a missing config there fails the build for a non-obvious reason.
tests
vitest.config.ts
.prettierrc.json
.prettierignore
*.tsbuildinfo

# Docs and deployment descriptors
docs
deploy
CICD.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.log
